From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 138/138] PC5: a media sample refuses a null buffer, so Sacred
 2 Remastered doesn't crash in its videos (Wine patch 1007)

---
 ...fplat-a-sample-refuses-a-null-buffer.patch | 26 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 wine/patches/1007-mfplat-a-sample-refuses-a-null-buffer.patch

diff --git a/wine/patches/1007-mfplat-a-sample-refuses-a-null-buffer.patch b/wine/patches/1007-mfplat-a-sample-refuses-a-null-buffer.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..61089bf
--- /dev/null
+++ b/wine/patches/1007-mfplat-a-sample-refuses-a-null-buffer.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
+Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH] mfplat: A sample refuses a null buffer.
+
+IMFSample::AddBuffer stored a null buffer and crashed taking its
+reference. Sacred 2 Remastered adds one during its videos when it
+couldn't make a frame's buffer, and crashed in mfplat. It now gets
+E_POINTER and goes on.
+---
+diff --git a/dlls/mfplat/sample.c b/dlls/mfplat/sample.c
+index 4d75924..d4ddba2 100644
+--- a/dlls/mfplat/sample.c
++++ b/dlls/mfplat/sample.c
+@@ -723,6 +723,11 @@ static HRESULT WINAPI sample_AddBuffer(IMFSample *iface, IMFMediaBuffer *buffer)
+ 
+     TRACE("%p, %p.\n", iface, buffer);
+ 
++    /* A null buffer is refused, not added: its reference crashed. Sacred 2
++     * Remastered adds one when it couldn't make a video frame's buffer. */
++    if (!buffer)
++        return E_POINTER;
++
+     EnterCriticalSection(&sample->attributes.cs);
+     if (!mf_array_reserve((void **)&sample->buffers, &sample->capacity, sample->buffer_count + 1,
+             sizeof(*sample->buffers)))
-- 
2.43.0

